    <main>
      <div class="about-grid">
        <div>
          <h1 class="page-title">I'm Chris Breuer. Passionately obsessed over developer tooling.</h1>
          <div class="prose">
            <p>
              Ever since I was young, I've loved to explore, learn, and create, especially
              while using tech. When I was 12 years old, I wrote my first SaaS app, and to
              my surprise it turned out quite successful and brought in several hundred
              dollars monthly via Google AdSense.
            </p>
            <p>
              The only thing I loved more than computers as a kid was sports and the
              outdoors. Almost 20 years later, not much has changed: going on hikes with my
              dogs and playing soccer are still some of the few things that peel me away
              from my desk.
            </p>
            <p>
              I spent the last 10+ years working on personal and private projects, ranging
              from small apps to large enterprise services, which caused my obsession with
              building scalable and serverless systems. I dove deep into data storage and
              transfer, and distributed and decentralized compute techniques. That was a
              core reason I started working on Stacks.
            </p>
            <p>
              Today, I'm the founder of <a href="https://stacksjs.com">Stacks</a> and a
              founding member of the <a href="https://ow3.org">Open Web Foundation</a>.
              It's exciting to work on the future of web technologies and application
              development. Follow along on <a href="https://github.com/chrisbbreuer">GitHub</a>
              for the latest updates.
            </p>
          </div>

